{
  // The browser-agent subtree is a SECOND, separate TypeScript program. It is not
  // part of the root `tsconfig.json` (which excludes `src/browserAgent`), and the
  // two configs disagree on purpose:
  //
  //  - `moduleResolution: "bundler"` — these sources are never emitted by tsc.
  //    `scripts/build-browser-agent.mjs` bundles them with esbuild into one IIFE,
  //    so a specifier only has to resolve at BUILD time, not at runtime. That is
  //    why the ~80 relative imports here are extensionless while every import
  //    under `src/` names a `.ts` file: the root program emits real Node ESM and
  //    needs `rewriteRelativeImportExtensions`, and this one has nothing to emit.
  //
  //  - `types: []` — the isolation that matters. Without it, tsc auto-includes
  //    `@types/node` and this browser code could reference `process`, `Buffer` or
  //    `__dirname` and typecheck clean, only to fail in a page. With it, those are
  //    errors. The subtree is Node-free today (no `node:` imports, no `require`)
  //    and this is what keeps it that way. `rrweb` and `@zumer/snapdom` are
  //    unaffected — they ship their own types, resolved through their imports.
  //
  //  - `lib` is explicit rather than inherited. The root program's ES2022 target
  //    resolves to `es2022.full`, which happens to include DOM; relying on that
  //    would mean browser code's DOM access depended on a Node program's target.
  //
  //  - No `verbatimModuleSyntax`. It is load-bearing in the root program for the
  //    forked method worker (see `scripts/assert-worker-standalone.mjs`) and means
  //    nothing here, where everything is bundled.
  //
  // `noEmit` because esbuild owns the output. This config exists to TYPECHECK;
  // `npm run typecheck` runs both programs.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2020",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2020", "DOM", "DOM.Iterable"],
    "types": [],
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true
  },
  "include": ["src/browserAgent"]
}
